# Tests of the generic group that guest/xfstests.sh does not run (global; the
# file system's own are in xfstests.<fstype>.excluded), each with the reason.
# One "generic/NNN <reason>" per line. A test that cannot apply to a FUSE file
# system is not listed: xfstests' own _require_* checks make it "not run". These
# are tests that cannot be run in this guest at all (they fail on the native
# file system too, or need a stand-alone coreutils program, or race an unmount
# against a mount of the same device). Tests that take most of the limit or
# more through dcfs are in xfstests.slow, not here.
generic/452 needs a stand-alone ls: Alpine's coreutils is one multi-call binary, and the test links to it under another name (fails natively too)
generic/478 fails on the native file system too: the test takes the semaphore key from ipcs and ipcmk, whose output differs here, so t_ofd_locks gets no file name
generic/570 acts on the raw scratch block device (mkswap, swapon, writes to the device under the file system): not applicable under dcfs, which serves the file system on it
generic/604 races an unmount in the background against a mount of the same device: it fails on ext4 about half the time because the previous dcfs daemon still holds the cache database (README.md, "Only one dcfs may use a cache database at a time")
generic/680 xfs_io is musl's and its getopt does not permute: `pwrite 0 4k -S 0xff` puts the option after the arguments, so the data is not written (fails natively too)
generic/749 xfs_io is musl's and its getopt does not permute: `$XFS_IO_PROG $file -c ...` takes -c as a file name ("-c: No such file or directory"; fails natively too)
